{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789758253,"nonce":"oild3x7oceKoRjoecfxH3RFTKFg=","title":"OSR resume inside nested loops needs phis at the dominance frontier, not only at the header","message":"osr::osr_layout_with repairs a live-in the resumed region redefines with one phi at the resume header (Repair, resumable). That is the right merge only when every path from the definition to a read passes the header; a read the definition reaches around the header (a three-level nest: the outermost counter read in the middle loop's body, entered both from the middle loop's back edge and from the outer loop through the middle header's pre-header) is rejected with RegionHasExternalEntry. Reproducer: an interpreted frame at the innermost header of a y/x/k nest (scratch nest3.py: for y, for x, while k) stays interpreted; the middle and outer headers still transfer. The complete fix places phis at the iterated dominance frontier of {prologue, definition block} in the helper's CFG (analysis::dominators::DominatorTree::frontier exists) and renames per dominance, at which point the rejection goes away.","files":null}]}